I've already reported this to the bug house.  But I thought I'd share
it with the net.

I've found that I really LIKE wandering around the dungeon polymorphed
into a Xorn.  You can walk through walls and it's very easy to get
away from pretty much any bad situation -- nothing but another Xorn
can follow you into the rock, you get three hits per turn, and if you
do encounter another Xorn, he's probably not carrying a weapon or
armor.   Further, lots of things are a lot easier - the stronghold
level is a snap.  It's easy to map the labyrinth; you can just sweep 
back and forth in a straight line until you find the stairs.  And
Heaven is great; you can just go around the big dragon filled room.

To be a Xorn, you just need a ring of polymorph and a ring of
polymorph control.  Xorns can wear hat, gloves, shoes and shield, so
you can be pretty well armored.

But there is a drawback.  Of the 4 times I've a Xorn, twice I've
gotten a program disorder that makes the game unplayable.  Suddenly,
when the screen is being redrawn, I get a flock of messages of the
form:

At gets a null at xx xx.
Program in disorder - perhaps you'd better quit.

where xx is a 2-digit number.  
  [I'm playing 3.0pl9 on a Sun workstation.]

I'm not suprised that this scenario generates some bugs -- after all,
the Xorn is the only creature that walks thru walls, and most players,
if they have polymorph and polycontrol, seem to favor master lichs and
vampire lords.

   But beware!

David Throop


